159 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 102 0 R
/E (Disputes over equity are a leading cause of startup failure. Many startup disputes do not arise because the business failed, rather, they arise because founders never agreed on ownership, roles, or expectations from the outset. Poorly structured equity arrangements can damage relationships, discourage investors, and even bring promising businesses to an end. Determining how equity should be shared is, therefore, one of the earliest and most important strategic decisions founders will make. While many founders assume that equity should be divided equally, an equal split is not always the fairest or the most commercially sensible approach. Equity holdings should reflect both present contributions and future commitment to the business.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
160 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 102 0 R
/E (When determining how to split equity between co-founders, the division does not necessarily have to be equal, as various factors influence how equity ownership is structured)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
161 0 obj
<<
