/P 102 0 R
/E (1.1     What is Equity? )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
162 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 903 0 R
/E (Equity simply represents ownership in a business. It determines who owns the company, who makes important decisions and who benefits when the business grows. Since early-stage startups often lack cash, they use equity to compensate founders, employees, and investors for the high risk they take. It provides stakeholders with voting rights, a claim to future profits, and decision-making influence.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
