381 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1032 0 R
/E (Vesting: This is the process of gaining the legal right to "exercise" or own your stock. It usually follows a linear schedule, where you earn a set portion of shares every month or year over a fixed period \(typically four or five years\). )
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
382 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1033 0 R
/E (The Cliff: This is a waiting period \(usually one year\) before any vesting happens. If an employee leaves before the cliff, they get zero shares; if they stay, they receive a "lump sum" of shares for that first year and then continue with the normal schedule.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
383 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1034 0 R
/E (Founder Vesting: Founders should also be subject to vesting arrangements, particularly where there are multiple co-founders. Founder vesting protects the company if a founder exits early while retaining a disproportionate ownership stake. This is now considered a standard investor practice and helps maintain long-term commitment and fairness within the founding team.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
384 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1035 0 R
