/T (Under Sections 305 and 306 of CAMA, directors are bound by fiduciary duties. They must act in good faith, prioritise the best interests of the company, and avoid conflicts of interest. In the context of equity, this means that issuing shares to insiders at below-market value, or favouring certain shareholders unfairly, can amount to a serious breach of duty with legal consequences.)
